<title>UK: Phytopharm makes progress on eczema medicine.</title>
<headline>Phytopharm makes progress on eczema medicine.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British medicine firm Phytopharm Plc said on Monday that it has been invited by the Medicines Control Agency to clarify further the programme of work required to register Zemaphyte, a medicine to treat atopic eczema.</p>
<p>Zemaphyte is a registered trademark of Phytopharm which specialises in herbal medicines.</p>
<p>Commenting on the invitation, Phytopharm said: &quot;We are encouraged that we have entered this next stage of the company's development&quot;.</p>
<p>The company said it would be in a position to announce the timetable for the programme of work in early 1997.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
